Zapier and Make both automate work between apps, but they bill in different units. Zapier counts **tasks**. Make counts **credits**. A plan that looks cheap on one site can cost more on the other once you count how many of those units your workflow uses. This guide compares the published prices as of 10 November 2026 and walks through three worked examples. It is based on the vendors' own documentation and pricing pages, not on our own use of either product, and both vendors write pages that favour their own product, so we show the numbers and the counting rules rather than their conclusions.

## Quick comparison

| | Zapier | Make |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Free plan | 100 tasks per month | 1,000 credits per month, no time limit |
| Entry paid plan | Professional, $19.99 per month billed annually, 750 tasks | Core, $9 per month (billing period not stated on Make's comparison page), 10,000 credits |
| Team plan | Team, $69 per month billed annually, 2,000 tasks, up to 25 users | Teams, $29 per month, from 10,000 credits (billing period not stated on Make's comparison page) |
| Unit billed | A completed action in another app | A module run that processes data |

Make's comparison page lists $9, $16 and $29 for these tiers without stating the billing period, and we could not confirm what the same plans cost on monthly billing, so check Make's live pricing page and its billing toggle before comparing. Zapier's figures above are the annual-billing prices from its own pricing articles; we did not verify Zapier's month-to-month prices.

## How Zapier counts usage

Zapier says a task is the work it performs in another app. According to Zapier, triggers, Filter and Paths steps, steps that error or halt, and built-in tools such as Looping and Delay do not count toward your task total, and its blog's examples treat Formatter steps as free too. Zapier's help article adds that successful steps inside an error-handler path do count. That matters for multi-step workflows: only the steps that act in your apps count.

If you go over your allowance, Zapier's paid plans keep running and bill the extra tasks. Zapier says annual plans pay 1.25 times the normal per-task cost for extra tasks, monthly plans pay 2.5 times, and total usage is capped at three times the plan's task limit. On Professional, that cap is 2,250 tasks in a month (750 included plus up to 1,500 extra).

## How Make counts usage

Make says each module that runs in a scenario typically counts as one credit. Some features use more. Make's own comparison page says modules that handle multiple data bundles or use its built-in AI tools may consume more than one credit, and Make's credits page says its built-in AI usage is priced by tokens. Make's help page says the Make Code app uses 2 credits per second of execution time. If you connect your own AI provider key, a Make community answer says the AI step costs one credit per run on Pro and above, while Make's credits page says paid plans, so confirm which applies to you.

Make sells extra credits if you run out, and its 6 November 2025 announcement changed how extra credits are priced, so check the current extra-credit rate on Make's pricing page before relying on overage as a budget. The same announcement moved plan limits: Core now tops out at 300,000 credits a month, and larger tiers sit on Pro.

## Three worked examples

These examples are our own arithmetic from the published numbers, not measured bills. They assume a workflow with a trigger and two actions in other apps. In Zapier that is 2 tasks per run. In Make we assume 3 credits per run, counting every module as one credit, which is the cautious case. Real usage varies with how many data bundles a module handles and whether you use AI modules.

### 200 runs a month

- Zapier: 400 tasks. This exceeds the Free plan's 100 tasks, and Zapier's blog lists two-step Zaps on the Free plan and multi-step workflows on Professional, so Free may not cover a trigger plus two actions either (confirm on Zapier's live page). It fits inside Professional's 750, so about $19.99 per month on annual billing.
- Make: 600 credits. This fits inside the Free plan's 1,000, so $0. Make's Academy says the free plan's minimum interval between scheduled runs is 15 minutes, and a Make how-to guide says the Free plan caps you at two active scenarios.

### 500 runs a month

- Zapier: 1,000 tasks. That is 250 over Professional's 750. Using Zapier's annual overage rule, the plan's normal task cost is about $0.0267 ($19.99 divided by 750), so each extra task is about $0.033, and 250 extra tasks come to roughly $8.33. Estimated total: about $28.32 per month. We calculated this ourselves from Zapier's stated multiplier, so confirm the exact charge in Zapier's calculator.
- Make: 1,500 credits. This is over the Free plan's 1,000, so the Core plan at $9 per month (billing period unconfirmed) covers it with 10,000 credits.

### 3,000 runs a month

- Zapier: 6,000 tasks. Professional's 2,250 figure is only the cap on pay-per-task overage for the 750-task tier, not a limit on the plan, so you would choose a larger task tier. Zapier's pricing page has a task selector for this, and we did not verify the price of tiers above 750, so we cannot give a Zapier total.
- Make: 9,000 credits. This fits inside Core's 10,000, so $9 per month (billing period unconfirmed).

The pattern is that Make's headline allowance is much larger per dollar. The caveat is that Make's count rises quickly if a workflow uses many modules, loops over many records or relies on built-in AI, and Zapier's count stays low if most of your steps are filters, formatting or paths.

## Which should you choose

Choose by counting your own steps. List the apps a typical run touches. For Zapier, count only the actions in other apps. For Make, count every module that processes data, then multiply by monthly runs. If the result fits the Free plan on one tool, start there. If you need teams, shared folders and roles, compare Zapier Team ($69 for up to 25 users) with Make Teams (from $29, billing period unconfirmed), and read the plan feature lists, since the included usage differs.

Both vendors change plans and prices. Make updated its plans on 6 November 2025, and Zapier restructured its plans during 2024. Check the live pricing pages before you commit, and note that this article was last verified on 10 November 2026.
